}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Bayara}}|area_km2=38,211|population_census=4,754,389|population_census_year=2025|regional_languages=|common_languages={{W|Aragonese language|Aragonese}}, [[Baliscano]], [[Kurupirangüe language|Kurupirangüe]]|cctld=.kma|mapsize=280px|population_census_rank=9th}}'''Camaca''' ({{Langx|kp|Kamakã|4=land of the [[w:pt:Camacãs|Kamakãs]]}}) is an autonomous [[Regions of Balisca|region]] of [[Bayara]], within the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]]. It is the southernmost region within the community, sharing borders with [[Carpinchera]] to the northwest, [[Jaguarundi]] to the south, [[Llaragón]] to the east, and [[Xaraba]] to the north.

Today, Camaca is distinctive for its vibrant tapestry of protected indigenous territories and urbanized cosmopolitan communities, fostering a rich cultural amalgamation that defines the regional identity. Outside of the administrative center, [[San Chorche]], the region's economy relies mainly on tourism (specifically {{W|ecotourism}}). 

